(obligation (id "OB-GC-COMPOSITION") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The profile's instruction set is RV64I plus the extensions M, A, F, D and C, plus Zicsr and Zifencei, plus Zicntr: 'G' is the defined abbreviation for the IMAFDZicsr_Zifencei base-and-extensions combination, and this profile is G plus C and Zicntr on the unprivileged side and Sstc on the privileged side.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-NAMING") (locator "36.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-GC-COMPOSITION"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-GC-COMPOSITION"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-GC-COMPOSITION") (required_checks "CHK-GC-COMPOSITION-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-COMPOSITION-NEG"))

(obligation (id "OB-EXT-CLOSURE") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The extension dependency closure is complete under the pinned revision: D depends on F; F depends on Zicsr for control and status register access; and C decomposes as Zca always plus Zcd when D is present (Zcf exists only at RV32). Nothing in this profile is inferred from the letter 'G' alone.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZC") (locator "28.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-NAMING") (locator "36.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-EXT-CLOSURE"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-EXT-CLOSURE"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-EXT-CLOSURE") (required_checks "CHK-EXT-CLOSURE-POS") (required_checks "CHK-EXT-CLOSURE-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-PRIV-REVISION") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The privileged architecture is the pinned publication's: Machine-Level ISA Version 1.13 and Supervisor-Level ISA Version 1.13, under spec revision v20260120 — the same publication family as the unprivileged pin.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-PRIV-REVISION"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-PRIV-REVISION"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-REVISION") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-REVISION-POS") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-REVISION-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-PRIV-MODES") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The profile implements machine, supervisor and user modes — the minimum a Linux-capable profile needs (M-mode firmware, S-mode kernel, U-mode userspace); the hypervisor extension is excluded, and every mode-dependent behaviour is tested in each supported mode (P4-SYSTEM.2).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INTRO") (locator "Introduction")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-PRIV-MODES"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-MODES-POS") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-MODES-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SV39") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Translation is Sv39: of the three paged virtual-memory schemes defined for SXLEN=64 (Sv39, Sv48, Sv57), the profile selects the minimal Linux-capable one — also the one the pinned SoC precedent implements (the FU540-C000's U54 supports Bare and Sv39). The U54's A/D behaviour (page faults instead of setting PTE A/D bits) is recorded as P4-SYSTEM.3's policy input, not as this profile's rule.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "§11.1.3–§11.1.4")) (source_refs (source_id "SIFIVE-FU540-C000") (locator "§4.7")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SV39"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SV39"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SV39") (required_checks "CHK-SV39-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SV39-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SVADE") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The profile implements Svade: when a translation needs an A or D PTE update, the hart raises a page fault instead of performing the hardware update. Three evidence legs: (i) the pinned revision defines exactly two A/D schemes and names the page-fault one Svade (RVP-SUPERVISOR §11.1.3.1, §11.1.10); (ii) the profile's own translation precedent — the U54 MMU the Sv39 choice already cites — implements exactly that scheme ('does not automatically set the A and D bits … Instead, the U54 MMU will raise a page fault', FU540 §4.7); (iii) the laboratory's observe-through-the-ISA discipline (P4-SYSTEM.2 decision 6) can evidence a page fault (scause/stval via csrr) but cannot evidence an implicit PTE write, so the hardware-update default would price a new observation vocabulary to test a side effect the laboratory need not produce. Svadu is NOT selected: menvcfg's ADUE stays WPRI (the state document's wpri_62_0 field).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "§11.1.3.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "§11.1.10")) (source_refs (source_id "SIFIVE-FU540-C000") (locator "§4.7")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SVADE"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SVADE"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SVADE") (required_checks "CHK-SVADE-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SVADE-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-FAULT-PRIORITY") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Synchronous exceptions follow the pinned priority table (decreasing priority): the instruction-address translation faults, then the instruction access fault, then illegal-instruction, environment call and environment break, then - the table's one implementation-defined position - load/store/AMO address-misaligned, which this profile takes HIGH, judged before the explicit access's translation (the laboratory's choice at P4-SYSTEM.3 decision 7; misaligned atomics take their declared access-fault codes at the same point), then the explicit access's translation faults (the first encountered), then its physical access fault. Instruction-address-misaligned is unreachable here (IALIGN 16 with C) and no breakpoint exists (no Sdtrig). Every adjacent pair the profile can produce is pinned by a guest on both engines: the fetch fault over decode (fault-fetch), illegal-instruction over misaligned and over translation faults (prio-sv39's FS=Off cells, f-fs-off, d-fs-off), misaligned over page and access faults (it-prio-load, prio-sv39, a-amo-sv39), translation over the physical access (prio-sv39).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "§2.1.1.15")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-FAULT-PRIORITY"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-FAULT-PRIORITY"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-FAULT-PRIORITY") (required_checks "CHK-FAULT-PRIORITY-POS") (required_checks "CHK-FAULT-PRIORITY-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-PARTIAL-PROGRESS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Every instruction completes or faults as a unit - the laboratory's declared preciseness (the pinned introduction leaves preciseness to the execution environment and recommends it): a delivered synchronous exception leaves the architectural state exactly as it was before the faulting instruction except for the trap report itself (xepc, xcause, xtval, the status stack, the mode, pc) - no x- or f-register, CSR, fflags, FS, reservation or memory write of the faulting instruction is committed. The reads that reached the environment before the fault are NOT rolled back and are declared, not hidden: a translation's earlier walk reads and its TLB fill, a page-straddling fetch's first parcel, and an atomic memory operation's completed load when its store is refused - each a read that changes no architectural state. No suboperation is restartable and no partial commit is possible. Positive fixtures: inj-carrier, inj-atomics, inj-fp, inj-walk-l2, inj-walk-l1, inj-walk-l0 (faults injected at a chosen suboperation through the typed carrier), mm-csr-ro-write, prio-sv39. Negative evidence: the parent engine fails mm-csr-ro-write (it committed rd and then trapped), and the corpus fails when the carrier is ignored or a refused walk read becomes a page fault.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "Exceptions, Traps, and Interrupts")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "§2.1.1.15")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-PARTIAL-PROGRESS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined"))) (param (name restartable_suboperations) (value (false))) (param (name partial_commit_possible) (value (false)))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-PARTIAL-PROGRESS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-PARTIAL-PROGRESS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-PARTIAL-PROGRESS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-IALIGN-16") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "With the C extension present, IALIGN is 16 — instructions start on any 16-bit boundary — while ILEN remains 32; no instruction-address-misaligned exception arises from C's 16-bit forms.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-C") (locator "27.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-IALIGN-16"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-IALIGN-16"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-IALIGN-16") (required_checks "CHK-IALIGN-16-POS") (required_checks "CHK-IALIGN-16-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ZICNTR") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The Zicntr base counters (cycle, time, instret) are included — explicitly beyond the G abbreviation — because a Linux-capable profile must offer the supervisor-mode time read; the counters' rate and progress semantics are the environment contract's to declare (P4-SYSTEM.5 and P4-SYSTEM.9), not this resolution's. Zihpm (hardware performance monitors) is not selected.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ZICNTR"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ZICNTR"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ZICNTR") (required_checks "CHK-ZICNTR-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ZICNTR-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SSTC") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Sstc is included — the supervisor timer-compare register stimecmp, gated by menvcfg.STCE — so an S-mode kernel programs its own timer without an M-mode round trip.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SSTC"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SSTC"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SSTC") (required_checks "CHK-SSTC-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SSTC-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-FP-DEFER") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "F and D are in the profile because the standard RV64G userspace ABI is LP64D, which requires the D extension; the model implements no floating point until the floating-point backend passes qualification (P4-SYSTEM.7), the CPU-SYSTEM gate verdict reads incomplete until then, and a Sail-versus-Spike floating-point comparison is one implementation twice (the SoftFloat shared ancestry), never independent numeric evidence.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-PSABI") (locator "§2.4–§2.5")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-FP-DEFER"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-FP-DEFER"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-FP-DEFER") (required_checks "CHK-FP-DEFER-POS") (required_checks "CHK-FP-DEFER-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ABI") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The toolchain ABI is LP64D — the standard RV64G ABI (ELFCLASS64 with EF_RISCV_FLOAT_ABI_DOUBLE, the hardware floating-point calling convention with ABI_FLEN=64); the toolchain is the host's clang/lld 21.1.8 with an rv64gc target (the existing guest-toolchain decision).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-PSABI") (locator "§2.4–§2.5")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ABI"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ABI"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ABI") (required_checks "CHK-ABI-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ABI-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SBI") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The firmware contract for the Linux boot route is SBI 2.0: compatible M-mode firmware provides selected SBI services (timer, console, system reset, hart state management) before entering the S-mode kernel — real firmware, and a host-modelled SBI is a different contract, never silently substituted.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-SBI") (locator "Chapters 4–12")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SBI"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SBI"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SBI") (required_checks "CHK-SBI-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SBI-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-CSR-SET") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The implemented CSR set is the committed minimum of 33: mhartid and misa; mstatus, mtvec, medeleg, mideleg, mie, mip, mscratch, mepc, mcause and mtval; menvcfg, mcounteren, mcycle and minstret; sstatus, stvec, sscratch, sepc, scause, stval, sie, sip and scounteren; satp; stimecmp; cycle, time and instret; and fflags, frm and fcsr. Per-CSR field semantics (WPRI/WARL/WLRL) belong to the privilege leaf (P4-SYSTEM.2).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-CSR") (locator "1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-CSR-SET"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-CSR-SET"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-CSR-SET") (required_checks "CHK-CSR-SET-POS") (required_checks "CHK-CSR-SET-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-NO-PMP") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "PMP is excluded at v0: the privileged architecture's physical memory protection unit is optional, and the first boot contract does not require it; the decision is revisited by the board branch that needs it.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "§2.1.7")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-NO-PMP"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-NO-PMP"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-NO-PMP") (required_checks "CHK-NO-PMP-POS") (required_checks "CHK-NO-PMP-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-NO-H") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The hypervisor extension is excluded: the profile has one hart and no virtualization workload in the first Linux profile; H would arrive with a consumer, never ahead of one.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INTRO") (locator "Introduction")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-NO-H"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-NO-H"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-NO-H") (required_checks "CHK-NO-H-POS") (required_checks "CHK-NO-H-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-RVWMO") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The memory consistency model is RVWMO: with the A extension in the profile the memory model is load-bearing even at one hart (the AMOs and their aq/rl annotations), and the multicore exposure of the weak model is MC-MULTICORE's, never smuggled in.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RVWMO") (locator "17.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-RVWMO"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-RVWMO"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-RVWMO") (required_checks "CHK-RVWMO-POS") (required_checks "CHK-RVWMO-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-PRIV-INSNS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The privileged instructions in scope are mret, sret, wfi and sfence.vma (the pinned privileged instruction listings); wfi's wake semantics belong to the interrupt/counter/wait leaf (P4-SYSTEM.5).") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INSNS") (locator "18.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-PRIV-INSNS"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-PRIV-INSNS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-PRIV-INSNS") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-INSNS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-PRIV-INSNS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-RESOLUTION-ROUTE") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "This unit is a profile resolution: the selection is exact and citable, and the definition pipeline (encoding fragments, semantics, guests) has not started; the dossier declares the profile-resolution vehicle route, and the definition-pipeline gates refuse any encoding, state-census or guest-corpus document beside the declaration.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "RISC-V Software Execution Environments and Harts")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-RESOLUTION-ROUTE"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-RESOLUTION-ROUTE"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-RESOLUTION-ROUTE") (required_checks "CHK-RESOLUTION-ROUTE-POS") (required_checks "CHK-RESOLUTION-ROUTE-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ROUTE-FLIP") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The definition pipeline has landed and the dossier declares the generated-definition vehicle route: the unit carries its encoding composition (the RV64I base plus Zicsr, Zicntr and the privileged-system fragment — (status partial) with six declared slots for M/A/F/D/C/Zifencei), the 33-CSR state document, the 62-guest corpus (the base mirror plus the mode matrix) and the 7-axis interaction matrix, and the generated mirrors (state_rv64gc.rs, definition_rv64gc.rs, guests_rv64gc.rs) are tracked because their canonical inputs are tracked in the same commit (decision_generated-mirror-needs-tracked-input).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "RISC-V Software Execution Environments and Harts")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ROUTE-FLIP"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ROUTE-FLIP"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ROUTE-FLIP") (required_checks "CHK-ROUTE-FLIP-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ROUTE-FLIP-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SCOPE-CENSUS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The scope block enumerates the RV64I base census (52 forms — the same enumeration and source as rv64i-lab-v0); each extension's instruction census lands with its encoding fragment in the evidence leaves (the RV32/64G listings and the privileged listings are the census references), and the declared scope grows only with them.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.4–§1.1.8")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.2–§3.1.3")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-G-LISTING") (locator "35.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INSNS") (locator "18.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SCOPE-CENSUS"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SCOPE-CENSUS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SCOPE-CENSUS") (required_checks "CHK-SCOPE-CENSUS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SCOPE-CENSUS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ALU-IMM") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "ADDI adds the sign-extended 12-bit immediate to rs1, wrapping modulo 2^XLEN; overflow is ignored. SLTI and SLTIU compare rs1 against the sign-extended immediate, signed and unsigned respectively — SLTIU still sign-extends the immediate first and then compares unsigned. XORI, ORI and ANDI are bitwise against the sign-extended immediate.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.4")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ALU-IMM"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ALU-IMM"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ALU-IMM") (required_checks "CHK-ALU-IMM-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ALU-IMM-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ALU-REG") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "ADD and SUB add and subtract modulo 2^XLEN; overflow is ignored and the result wraps. SLT and SLTU are signed and unsigned comparisons respectively, producing 0 or 1. XOR, OR and AND are bitwise.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.4")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ALU-REG"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ALU-REG"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ALU-REG") (required_checks "CHK-ALU-REG-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ALU-REG-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ECALL-EBREAK") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "ECALL and EBREAK cause a precise REQUESTED trap to the execution environment. With no privileged modes in this profile there is no guest handler, so both are reported to the harness as a typed environment-trap outcome and execution stops unless the harness contract says otherwise.") (authority implementation-profile) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.8")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "Exceptions/Traps/Interrupts (Requested Trap)")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ECALL-EBREAK"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ECALL-EBREAK"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ECALL-EBREAK") (required_checks "CHK-ECALL-EBREAK-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ECALL-EBREAK-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ENDIAN") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Little-endian. The specification delegates this to the EEI; endianness in RISC-V is byte-address invariant.") (authority implementation-profile) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.6")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ENDIAN"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ENDIAN"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ENDIAN") (required_checks "CHK-ENDIAN-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ENDIAN-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-FENCE") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "FENCE is decoded and must not trap. With one hart, no external devices and an in-order model, it has no observable effect. FENCE.TSO (fm=1000, pred=RW, succ=RW) is accepted and treated as FENCE RW,RW, which the specification states is correct. The remaining fm, pred and succ configurations are reserved, and the architecture SPECIFIES their behavior: base implementations shall treat all such reserved configurations as FENCE instructions (with fm = 0000) — they decode and execute as an ordinary FENCE, which under this profile has no observable effect. They do NOT fall under D-RESERVED-DECODE, and the rs1 and rd fields are ignored for forward compatibility, as the same section directs.") (authority implementation-profile) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.7, Table 3 Fence mode encoding")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-FENCE"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-FENCE"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-FENCE") (required_checks "CHK-FENCE-POS") (required_checks "CHK-FENCE-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-JALR-LSB") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "JALR computes its target by adding the sign-extended 12-bit immediate to rs1 and then setting the least-significant bit of the result to zero.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.5.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-JALR-LSB"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-JALR-LSB"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-JALR-LSB") (required_checks "CHK-JALR-LSB-POS") (required_checks "CHK-JALR-LSB-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-LOAD-EXT") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "LW sign-extends its 32-bit result to 64 bits; LWU zero-extends it. LH/LB sign-extend and LHU/LBU zero-extend analogously. SD/SW/SH/SB store the low 64/32/16/8 bits of rs2.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.3")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-LOAD-EXT"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-LOAD-EXT"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-LOAD-EXT") (required_checks "CHK-LOAD-EXT-POS") (required_checks "CHK-LOAD-EXT-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-LOAD-X0") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "A load with rd = x0 must still raise any exceptions and cause any other side effects, even though the loaded value is discarded.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.6")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-LOAD-X0"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-LOAD-X0"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-LOAD-X0") (required_checks "CHK-LOAD-X0-POS") (required_checks "CHK-LOAD-X0-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-LUI-AUIPC") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "LUI places the 32-bit U-immediate in rd with the low 12 bits zeroed, sign-extended to 64 bits. AUIPC forms the same 32-bit offset, sign-extends it to 64 bits, and adds it to the address of the AUIPC instruction.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.2.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-LUI-AUIPC"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-LUI-AUIPC"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-LUI-AUIPC") (required_checks "CHK-LUI-AUIPC-POS") (required_checks "CHK-LUI-AUIPC-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-NO-DELAY-SLOTS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Control transfers have no architecturally visible delay slots.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV32I") (locator "§1.1.5")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-NO-DELAY-SLOTS"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-NO-DELAY-SLOTS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-NO-DELAY-SLOTS") (required_checks "CHK-NO-DELAY-SLOTS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-NO-DELAY-SLOTS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SHAMT") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "SLLI/SRLI/SRAI take a 6-bit shift amount from the I-immediate; SLL/SRL/SRA use only the low 6 bits of rs2. SLLIW/SRLIW/SRAIW take 5 bits, and SLLW/SRLW/SRAW use rs2[4:0].") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.2.1, §3.1.2.2")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SHAMT"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SHAMT"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SHAMT") (required_checks "CHK-SHAMT-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SHAMT-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-WSUFFIX") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The *W instructions ignore the upper 32 bits of their inputs, produce a 32-bit signed result, and sign-extend it to 64 bits — bits XLEN-1 through 31 are equal. Overflow is ignored.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.2, §3.1.2.1, §3.1.2.2")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-WSUFFIX"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-WSUFFIX"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-WSUFFIX") (required_checks "CHK-WSUFFIX-POS") (required_checks "CHK-WSUFFIX-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-XLEN") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "XLEN = 64. The integer registers and the supported user address space are 64 bits.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RV64I") (locator "§3.1.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-XLEN"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-XLEN"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined"))) (param (name mirrored_from) (value (str "rv64i-lab-v0")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-XLEN") (required_checks "CHK-XLEN-POS") (required_checks "CHK-XLEN-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-CSR-ACCESS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The Zicsr instructions atomically read and write the addressed CSR under the uniform permission model: csrrw swaps, csrrs sets bits, csrrc clears bits, and the immediate forms use the zero-extended 5-bit uimm; csrrw/csrrwi with rd=x0 do not read the CSR; csrrs/csrrc with rs1=x0 and csrrsi/csrrci with uimm=0 do not write it. An access below the address's privilege level, a write to a read-only address, a counter read gated off by mcounteren (and scounteren in U), an stimecmp access below M with mcounteren.TM=0 or menvcfg.STCE=0, and a satp access in S with mstatus.TVM=1 each raise an illegal-instruction exception.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICSR") (locator "5.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-CSR") (locator "1.1.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-CSR-ACCESS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-CSR-ACCESS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-CSR-ACCESS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-CSR-ACCESS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-PRIV-INSNS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The privileged system instructions behave per mode: mret/sret execute in their mode or higher and raise illegal-instruction below it (sret also raises in S when mstatus.TSR=1); wfi executes as a no-op when legal (the specification's own latitude), raises illegal-instruction in U (S is present), and in S when mstatus.TW=1; sfence.vma raises illegal-instruction in U and in S with mstatus.TVM=1, and its invalidation effect is a stated no-op at this stage (no translation caches are modelled; Sv39 is P4-SYSTEM.3). xRET pops the two-level privilege stack (xIE<-xPIE, mode<-xPP, xPIE<-1, xPP<-U), clears MPRV when the target is not M, and sets pc<-xepc.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INSNS") (locator "18.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.3.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.3.3")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1.2.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-PRIV-INSNS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-PRIV-INSNS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-PRIV-INSNS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-PRIV-INSNS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-COUNTERS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The Zicntr counter reads rdcycle/rdtime/rdinstret read the cycle/time/instret values into rd; they are csrrs specializations (rs1=x0, the counter's address) and obey the counter-enable gates: below M the read is legal only with the mcounteren bit, and in U additionally the scounteren bit; the counters' rate and progress are the environment contract's (P4-SYSTEM.5/.9).") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.1.11")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1.1.5")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-COUNTERS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-COUNTERS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-COUNTERS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-COUNTERS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-WALK-IMPLICIT") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "When address translation is active (satp.MODE=Sv39), the hart's implicit memory accesses are the instruction fetch AND the translation algorithm's page-table reads: up to LEVELS (3) implicit 8-byte reads per access, each crossing the environment boundary as the walk-access kind, never silently as a data load. Under Svade the permitted page-table side effects are NONE: no implicit writes, ever. This AMENDS the implicit-access vocabulary for the translated composition: the base corpus's REQ-D-FETCH-IMPLICIT stays true of rv64i-lab-v0 (no translation exists there), and rv64gc's catalogue never carried it — measured: the mirror's closure is 13 records and it is not among them.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "§11.1.3.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "Memory")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-WALK-IMPLICIT"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-WALK-IMPLICIT"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-WALK-IMPLICIT") (required_checks "CHK-WALK-IMPLICIT-POS") (required_checks "CHK-WALK-IMPLICIT-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-ATOMICS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The A extension's 22 forms behave per the pinned chapter: LR loads the word or doubleword and registers the reservation (sign-extended for .W); SC conditionally stores and writes the code to rd — 0 on success, 1 on failure under the declared deterministic policy; the nine AMOs read-modify-write atomically at both widths — the old memory value to rd (sign-extended for .W), the computed value to memory, one store/AMO-rules translation (an AMO on an unreadable page raises a store page fault, never a load page fault). The aq/rl annotations decode (all four combinations) and order nothing observable at one hart.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.4")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-ATOMICS"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-ATOMICS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ATOMICS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ATOMICS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-FENCEI") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "fence.i retires as a no-op with no observable effect and never traps: the instruction-fetch synchronization is already provided by construction — this machine re-reads memory on every fetch, so a store to a later-fetched address is visible to the next fetch immediately (the laboratory's declared choice, D-CODE-VISIBILITY), and the chapter's coherent/uncached-RAM latitude ('just the fetch pipeline needs to be flushed at a FENCE.I') leaves nothing to flush. The instruction's funct12/rs1/rd fields are decoded and IGNORED — a fence.i word with nonzero fields executes, never raises (the chapter's forward-compatibility rule: base implementations shall ignore these fields); standard software zeroes them.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZIFENCEI") (locator "4.1")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-FENCEI"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-FENCEI") (required_checks "CHK-GC-FENCEI-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-FENCEI-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-F") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The F extension's 30 single-precision forms behave per the pinned chapter under IEEE 754-2008: every rounded operation rounds by its static rm field or, for DYN (111), by frm; a reserved rounding mode (a static 101/110, or DYN while frm holds 101-111) is an illegal-instruction exception that writes nothing; the five exception flags accrue sticky in fflags, with tininess detected after rounding; every NaN an arithmetic operation produces is the canonical NaN 0x7fc00000, while the transfers, sign injection and the bit moves keep the bits; because D is present every single-precision value lives NaN-boxed in its 64-bit register and an input that is not properly boxed reads as the canonical NaN; the float-to-integer conversions round by the mode and saturate out-of-range and NaN inputs with NV per the chapter's table; and with mstatus.FS Off every F instruction is an illegal-instruction exception, while FS becomes Dirty whenever an f-register or the accrued flags change (the declared Precise rule).") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.3")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.4")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.6")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.7")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.1.6.7")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-F"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-F") (required_checks "CHK-GC-F-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-F-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-D") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The D extension's 32 double-precision forms behave as their single-precision counterparts at format 64, as the pinned chapter defines them: rounding by the static rm or, for DYN, frm, a reserved rounding mode an illegal-instruction exception even on an operation that cannot round (FCVT.D.W[U], FCVT.D.S); the five flags accrue sticky; every NaN an arithmetic operation produces is the canonical NaN 0x7ff8000000000000; FLD/FSD and FMV.X.D/FMV.D.X move the 64 bits unmodified, so a NaN-boxed single read by a D operation is the negative quiet NaN it appears as; FCVT.S.D rounds by rm and writes its single NaN-boxed, FCVT.D.S widens exactly and reads its operand through the boxing rule (an unboxed input is the canonical NaN); a signaling-NaN input to a conversion raises NV; the integer conversions saturate with NV as FCVT.int.S does; and every D instruction is an illegal-instruction exception at mstatus.FS Off, with FS Dirty on any f-register write or flag change.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1.3")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1.4")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1.5")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1.6")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1.7")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.1.6.7")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-D"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-D") (required_checks "CHK-GC-D-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-D-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-RESERVATION") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The hart's reservation is one (physical address, width, valid) of the most recent LR — the minimal conformant reservation set (exactly the accessed word's or doubleword's bytes, RVI-A §12.1.2, the latitude the same section grants), keyed on the physical address (the aliasing latitude resolved to exact physical match). Invalidation is exactly the specification's one-hart set: any LR replaces; any SC — success or failure, any address — clears; a trap does NOT invalidate (the SC's own trap included).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.2")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-RESERVATION"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-RESERVATION"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-RESERVATION") (required_checks "CHK-RESERVATION-POS") (required_checks "CHK-RESERVATION-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-SC-DETERMINISTIC") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Store-conditional is deterministic: SC succeeds iff the reservation is valid and the physical address equals and the width equals, writing rs2's value and rd<-0; otherwise it fails with rd<-1 (the 'unspecified failure' code), writing nothing; it NEVER spuriously fails — one legal point of the architectural nondeterminism (RVI-A §12.1.2–§12.1.3 permits unconditional failure of unconstrained sequences), chosen so exact-value expectations stay derivable (EVD-05).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.3")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-SC-DETERMINISTIC"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-SC-DETERMINISTIC"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-SC-DETERMINISTIC") (required_checks "CHK-SC-DETERMINISTIC-POS") (required_checks "CHK-SC-DETERMINISTIC-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-ATOMIC-MISALIGN") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v0") (contract_version "0") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Misaligned atomic accesses take the access-fault family by kind — 5 for LR (a load exception: RVP-MACHINE's exception table maps load-reserved to load exceptions), 7 for SC/AMO (store/AMO exceptions): the specification offers misaligned-or-access-fault (RVI-A §12.1.2, §12.1.4) and the choice is reference-matched to the tracked Sail override's declared PMAs ((amo AccessFault) (lrsc AccessFault)); judged before translation (the P4-SYSTEM.3 decision-7 hand-off).") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.4")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-D-ATOMIC-MISALIGN"))) (param (name decision_id) (value (str "D-ATOMIC-MISALIGN"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "implementation-defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-D-ATOMIC-MISALIGN") (required_checks "CHK-ATOMIC-MISALIGN-POS") (required_checks "CHK-ATOMIC-MISALIGN-NEG"))
